<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Having seen the dead lying about (Things.Corpse.GiveObservedThought, via Thoughts.PawnObserver). Their own
    file rather than entries in Thoughts_Memories.xml, per CLAUDE.md: DefLoader reads every file under a Def
    folder, so additive content never has to edit a shared one.

    RimWorld 1.0's Defs are not in the decompile this port reads from, so every number below is RECALLED, not
    sourced, and is pinned by ObservationTests as a band and a trend rather than by the literal: a fresh body is
    a bad moment and a rotting one is a worse one (both negative, rotting stronger); neither is the kind of
    wound that outlasts the cause (both fade inside a day once the pawn stops seeing the body); and the
    penalty a settlement carries grows with how many bodies lie in sight but never runs away.
      - baseMoodEffect -4 (fresh) and -6 (rotting): recalled as RimWorld 1.0's Thoughts_Memory_Misc values.
      - durationDays 0.25: recalled as the same. A body that stays in view keeps renewing it
        (Thought_MemoryObservation), so what fades is the memory of a body that has been taken away or that
        the pawn has walked away from - the recovery the settlement has to wait out.
      - nullifyingTraits Psychopath + Bloodlust: the pair this port's WitnessedDeathAlly already names for the
        same reason (people who are not disturbed by death). Recalled for RimWorld's own defs, unverified.
      - stackLimit 100: UNSOURCED for RimWorld, and chosen to be inert. Thought_MemoryObservation merges by
        target and RimWorld never enforces the stack limit on it; this port's MemoryThoughtHandler enforces
        every def's limit after an add, so the limit has to be one the observer can never reach. A look samples
        PawnObserver.SampleNumCells (100) cells, so at most 100 distinct bodies can be seen at once, and a
        limit of 100 can never evict a body that is still in view. The mood a crowd of bodies costs is bounded
        by stackedEffectMultiplier (the mood sum of n alike thoughts approaches 1/(1-m) times one of them),
        not by this.
      - stackedEffectMultiplier: left at the default 0.75 (RimWorld's ThoughtDef default).
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>ObservedLayingCorpse</defName>
    <thoughtClass>SimWorld.Thoughts.Thought_MemoryObservation</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>0.25</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>100</stackLimit>
    <nullifyingTraits>
      <li>Psychopath</li>
      <li>Bloodlust</li>
    </nullifyingTraits>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>observed corpse</label>
        <description>There is a dead body lying around. It is disturbing.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>ObservedLayingRottingCorpse</defName>
    <thoughtClass>SimWorld.Thoughts.Thought_MemoryObservation</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>0.25</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>100</stackLimit>
    <nullifyingTraits>
      <li>Psychopath</li>
      <li>Bloodlust</li>
    </nullifyingTraits>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>observed rotting corpse</label>
        <description>There is a rotting body lying around. It is revolting.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-6</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
